pital\n69 Union Bank of India | Integrated Annual Report 2025-26\nGRI Index Capitals Strategy About\nISSB S2 — Climate-related Disclosures\nDisclosure Requirement Section/Sub-section Key Metric\nPhysical & Transition risks\nClimate-related risks & opportunities Natural Capital — Climate Risk Management Framework\nFive high-emission sectors","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · FY2026","document_date":null,"document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c1066","section":"Corporate Governance","tag":"governance","page":422,"text":"Five high-emission sectors\nClimate scenario analysis Natural Capital — Stress Testing | High-Impact Sector Analysis\nFinanced emissions (Scope 3 Category 15) Natural Capital — PCAF Methodology PCAF First-Mover in India\nNet-Zero 2035\nTransition plan Natural Capital — Strategic Pillars for Climate Leadership\nIndustry-based metrics — Green Finance Natural Capital — Green Finance Portfolio ` 37,435 Crore portfolio\nUnder Implementation\nPhysical risk metrics Natural Capital — Lat/Long Physical Risk Assessment\nTNFD — Taskforce on Nature-related Financial Disclosures\nTNFD Pillar Disclosure Requirement Bank's Status\nESG Steering Committee | RMC\nGovernance Board oversight of nature-related risks and opportunities\nStrategy Nature-related dependencies, risks & opportunities Nature risk assessment under scoping\nRisk & Impact Management Identification, assessment & management of nature- related risks\nESDD (Environmental Social Due Diligence) framework\nMetrics & Targets Metrics to measure, monitor & manage nature-related dependencies\nNature-positive financing frameworks — under development\nUN SDG Alignment — FY 2025–26\nUN SDG Goal Bank's Contribution — FY 2025–26\nSDG 1 No Poverty PMJDY 3.40 crore accounts | SHG lending ` 33,212 Cr | Mudra ` 20,311 Cr\nSDG 2 Zero Hunger Agriculture credit ` 1,83,394 Cr | KCC 2.58 lakh | SMF ` 97,787 Cr","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · FY2026","document_date":null,"docum