"section":"Corporate Governance","tag":"governance","page":516,"text":"DPC - Disciplinary Proceedings Committee – Vigilance/Non-vigilance\nSTCB - Share Transfer Committee of the Board\nHRSC - Human Resource Sub-Committee of the Board\nITSC - Information Technology Strategy Committee\nMCB - Management Committee of the Board\nNRC - Nomination & Remuneration Committee\nRCBWD - Review Committee of the Board for Willful Defaulters\n-\nREMC\nRecovery Management Committee of the Board\n-\nBCCS\nBoard Committee for Compromise Settlements\n2.7 Appointments/Cessations during the Financial Year 2025-26:\nAppointments: The following new directors inducted on the Board during the financial year 2025-26: -\nExpiry date of\nNature of\nBrief Profile\nSr. No.\nName Age Date of Appointment\ncurrent term\nExpertise\n52 11.04.2025 One year from\nAudit, Taxation &\n1. Shri Suraj Srivastava\nShri Suraj Srivastava is a Fellow Member of The Institute of Chartered Accountants of India (ICAI) and a Bachelor of Laws (LL.B.). Shri Srivastava has a rich professional experience of over 16 years as a practicing Chartered Accountant in taxation and audit practice.\nFinance\nthe date of notification i.e.\nApril 11, 2025, or until further orders, whichever\nis earlier\n54 30.09.2025 Three years or\nCredit, Credit\n2. Shri Asheesh Pandey","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · FY2026","document_date":null,"document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c1346","section":"Corporate Governance","tag":"governance","page":516,"text":"2. Shri Asheesh Pandey\nShri Asheesh Pandey is a seasoned Banker with experience of more than 27 years. He started his career from erstwhile Corporation Bank. Prior to assuming the current position, he worked as an Executive Director of the Bank of Maharashtra and Chief General Manager of the Union Bank of India. Shri Pandey has an experience of handling diverse portfolio ranging from Credit, Credit Monitoring, Treasury & Merchant Banking, Foreign Transactions & Joint Ventures, Marketing & Customer Relationships and Banking Operations. Being a Tech-Savvy banker, he has played a key role in successful digital banking transformation by adopting ideations and innovations. He has also played an important role in the re-engineering, harmonization.\nuntil further\nMonitoring,\norders\nTreasury &\nMerchant Banking, Foreign\nTransactions &\nJoint Ventures,\nMarketing & Customer Relationships\nand Banking\nOperations\n164 Union Bank of India | Integrated Annual Report 2025-26\nFinancials Reports Notice\nExpiry date of\nNature of\nBrief Profile\nSr. No.\nName Age Date of Appointment\ncurrent term\nExpertise\nFinance, IT and\n3. Shri Rohan Chand Thakur\n40 24.07.2025 Until further orders","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · FY2026","document_date":null,"document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c1347","section":"Corporate Governance","tag":"governance","page":517,"text":"40 24.07.2025 Until further orders\nShri Rohan Chand Thakur is an officer of Indian Administrative Service (IAS) belonging to 2009 batch of Himachal Pradesh Cadre. At present, he is working as Director in Ministry of Finance, Department of Financial Services, Government of India. He is an economics graduate from St. Stephen’s College, Delhi and a Postgraduate in Management from IIM Ahmedabad. Experience in Government of Himachal Pradesh:\nTaxation\ni. District Collector of Hamirpur and Shimla.\nii. Director of Information Technology.\niii. Managing Director of Skill Development\n& Entrepreneurship Department.\niv. Managing Director of Himachal Pradesh\nFinancial Corporation,\nv. Excise and Taxation Commissioner.\nvi. Managing Director of Himachal Road\nTransport Corporation.\nHe has previously worked with TAS before joining the civil services. He is also a Chevening Gurukul Fellow from the University of Oxford and a Master of Public Administration from Harvard Kennedy School, Harvard University, Cambridge, Massachusetts.\nCorporate Credit,","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · FY2026","document_date":null,"document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c1348","section":"Corporate Governance","tag":"governance","page":517,"text":"Corporate Credit,\nPrior to assuming the office as the Executive Director of Union Bank of India, Shri Amresh Prasad was the Chief General Manager of Punjab National Bank posted at corporate office. He has rich banking experience of over 32 years from branch banking, Zonal Offices to Head Office level, which includes Corporate Credit, Credit Review and Monitoring, Transaction Monitoring etc. He is a graduate in Chemistry and Certified Associate from Indian Institute of Bankers (CAIIB). Shri Prasad has attended various training and Leadership Development Programs and has taken part in Leadership Development Program at SBIL Kolkata. He has also completed Aarohan 2023 FSIB Program conducted by Financial Services Institution.\n4. Shri Amresh Prasad\n57 24.11.2025 Three years from the date of assumption of office i.e., 24th November 2022 or till the date of his attaining the age of superannuation i.e., 31.10.2028 or until further orders, whichever is earlier\nCredit Review and Monitoring,\nTransaction\nMonitoring\n165 Union Bank of India | Integrated Annual Report 2025-26\nGRI Index Capitals Strategy About\nCorporate Governance Report\nExpiry date of\nNature of\nBrief Profile\nSr. No.\nName Age Date of Appointment\ncurrent term\nExpertise","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · FY2026","document_date":null,"document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c1349","section":"Corporate Governance","tag":"governance","page":518,"text":"Expertise\nDr. Debasish Prusty is a member of the Indian Administrative Service and now serving as the Additional Secretary in the Department of Financial Services in the Union Ministry of Finance in the Government of India. He has more than 26 years of experience in the designing and implementing polices in the realm of Public Finance, Sustainable Development, and Development Cooperation and Environmental and Urban Governance. He had contributed to India’s initiative for collaboration and partnership with various countries to launch the International Solar Alliance (ISA) platform in the year 2015 when he was the Director in the Climate change division of the Ministry of Environment, Forest and Climate Change in Government of India. In the international negotiations in the conference of parties held under the United Nations Conference on Climate Change (UNFCCC) he had represented India’s negotiating team. He was a member of the standing committee on Finance of the UNFCCC in 2016. He has been conferred the Doctor of Philosophy from the Management Department of the Manipal University Jaipur and the Master of philosophy in Environmental sciences from the Jawaharlal Nehru University, Delhi, India. Dr. Prusty is well trained from the International Monetary Fund (IMF) in the field of Finance for Macro-economists. *Dr. Debasish Prusty Nominated as Government Nominee Director vice Shri Rohan Chand Thakur on 13.05.2026.","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · FY2026","document_date":null,"document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c1350","section":"Corporate Governance","tag":"governance","page":518,"text":"5. Dr. Debasish Prusty\n49 13.05.2026* Until further orders\nFinance & Management,\nBanking\nCessations: The following members ceased to be the Directors during the financial year 2025-26:\nNo. Name of Director Designation Date of\nSr.\nCessation Reason\n1. Ms. A. Manimekhalai Managing Director & CEO 02.06.2025 Completion of Tenure\n2. Shri Pankaj Dwivedi Executive Director 24.06.2025 Appointment cancelled by the Central Government\n24.07.2025 GOI nominated Shri Rohan Chand Thakur in place\n3. Shri Sameer Shukla Government Nominee\nof Shri Sameer Shukla\nDirector\n06.11.2025 Completion of Tenure\n4. Shri Srinivasan\nNon-Executive Chairman\nVaradarajan,\nand Part-Time Non-\nOfficial Director