025-26 dated 23.05.2025\nhas imposed penalty of ` 63,60,000/-(Rupees Sixty Three lakh and Sixty Thousand only) on the bank for failing to transfer\nDEA Fund in a timely manner and for obtaining collateral for agricultural loans up to ` 1.60 lakh, in contravention of\nregulatory guidelines.\n3. The RBI, Enforcement Department, vide Order Reference No. CO.ENFD.DECB.No.S820/02-01-018/2025-26 dated","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · FY2026","document_date":null,"document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c1607","section":"Cash Flow Statement","tag":"cashflow","page":629,"text":"3. The RBI, Enforcement Department, vide Order Reference No. CO.ENFD.DECB.No.S820/02-01-018/2025-26 dated\n27.03.2026, has imposed a penalty of ` 95,40,000 (Rupees Ninety-Five Lakh Forty Thousand only) on the Bank on account of\nnon-compliances, namely failure to credit (shadow reversal) the amount involved in unauthorized electronic transactions\nto certain customers’ accounts within 10 working days from the date of notification by the customer, failure to provide\ncustomers with 24x7 access to report unauthorized banking transactions through multiple channels, and resorting to\nmanual intervention in the system-based asset classification process in certain KCC accounts, in contravention of regulatory\nguidelines.\nAccordingly, penalty of ` 37,00,000/- was paid on 21.04.2025, ` 63,60,000/- was paid on 02.06.2025 and ` 95,40,000 was\npaid on 04.04.2026.\n13. KEY MANAGEMENT PERSONNEL -REMUNERATION PAID\n(` in crore)\nParticulars Designation FY 2025-26\nShri Asheesh Pandey Managing Director & CEO (from 30.09.2025) 0.22\nShri Nitesh Ranjan Executive Director 0.45\nShri Ramasubramanian S Executive Director 0.56\nShri Sanjay Rudra Executive Director 0.37\nShri Amresh Prasad Executive Director (from 24.11.2025) 0.16\nTotal 1.76\n277 Union Bank of India | Integrated Annual Report 2025-26\nGRI Index Capitals Strategy About\nSchedule 18 – Notes to Accounts\n14. OTHER DISCLOSURES\na. Business Ratios:","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · FY2026","document_date":null,"document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c1608","section":"Cash Flow Statement","tag":"cashflow","page":630,"text":"a. Business Ratios:\nParticulars FY 2025-26 FY 2024-25\nS. No.\nI. Interest Income as a percentage to Working Funds # 7.06% 7.44%\nII. Non-interest income as a percentage to Working Funds # 1.29% 1.39%\nIII. Cost of Deposit 5.39% 5.53%\nIV. Net Interest Margin * 2.70% 2.91%\nV. Operating Profit as a percentage to Working Funds # 1.91% 2.18%\nVI. Return on Assets $ 1.25% 1.26%\nVII. Average Business (Deposits plus advances) per employee (` in Crore) @ 29.45 28.02\nVIII. Net Profit per employee (` in Crore) 0.25 0.24\n# Working funds to be reckoned as average of total assets (excluding accumulated losses, if any) as reported to RBI in Form X for\nCommercial Banks during the 12 months of the financial year.\n* Net Interest Margin = Net Interest Income / Average Interest Earning Assets Where Net Interest Income = Interest Income –\nInterest Expense.\n$ Return on Assets would be with reference to average working funds (i.e., total of assets excluding accumulated losses, if any).\n@ For the purpose of computation of business per employee (deposits plus advances), inter-bank deposits shall be excluded.\nb. Bancassurance Business:\nThe breakup of income derived from bancassurance business is given here below:\n(` in crore)\nNature of Income FY 2025-26 FY 2024-25\n1. Life Insurance Policies 396.72 445.73\n2. Non-Life Insurance Policies 38.09 36.24\n3. Health Insurance 40.64 50.85\nc. Marketing and distribution:","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · FY2026","document_date":null,"document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c1609","section":"Cash Flow Statement","tag":"cashflow","page":630,"text":"c. Marketing and distribution:\nThe details of fees / remuneration received in respect of the marketing and distribution function (excluding\nbancassurance business) are as follows:\n(` in crore)\nNature of Income FY 2025-26 FY 2024-25\nDistributing Mutual Fund Business 29.66 27.48\nMerchant Banking Division 6.00 7.45\n278 Union Bank of India | Integrated Annual Report 2025-26\nFinancials Reports Notice\nd. Priority Sector Lending Certificate\nOther income of the Bank inter alia includes commission income of ` 133.87 Crore (PY ` 955.08 crore) from sale of Priority\nSector Lending Certificate under PSLC-SFMF category and an expenditure of ` 0.50* Crore (PY ` 236.70 Crores) through\npurchase of priority sector lending certificate under PSLC - General category.\nTraded value of PSLC certificate during the year are given below: (` in crore)\nCommission\nCommission\nPSLC-category PSLC Sold PSLC Purchased\nEarned\npaid*\nPSLC-SFMF 10,000 -- 133.87 --\nPSLC-Agriculture -- -- -- --\nPSLC-Micro -- -- -- --\nPSLC-General -- 5,000 -- 0.50*\nTOTAL 10,000 5,000 133.87 0.50*\n*excl. GST\ne. Provision & Contingencies\n(` in crore)\nBreak up of Provision & Contingencies debited to Profit & Loss Account: FY 2025-26 FY 2024-25\nProvision / (Reversal) for NPI on Investment 123.53 (101.28)\nProvision towards NPA 2,337.25 7,308.49\nProvision/(Reversal) towards Standard Assets 1,145.63 81.28","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · FY2026","document_date":null,"document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c1610","section":"Cash Flow Statement","tag":"cashflow","page":631,"text":"Provision/(Reversal) towards Standard Assets 1,145.63 81.28\nNet Provision made towards Income Tax (IT)/ Deferred tax assets (DTA) 5,483.91 5,491.92\nOther Provision and Contingencies:\n--\n--\n- Shifting Loss\n(26.61)\n(2.02)\n- Restructured Advances\n349.10\n834.06\n- Others\nTOTAL 9,922.36 13,102.90\nf. Implementation of IFRS converged Indian Accounting Standards (Ind AS)\nThe RBI vide circular DBR.BP.BC.No. 76/21.07.001/2015-16 dated 11th February 2016, has prescribed the roadmap for\nimplementation of Indian Accounting Standards (Ind-AS) in the Banks and the Banks needs to disclose the strategy for Ind-\nAS implementation, including the progress made in this regard. Further RBI vide circular DBR.BP.BC.No. 29/21.07.001/2018-\n19 dated 22nd March 2019 deferred implementation of IND AS till further notice.\nThe Bank, accordingly, has appointed a Consultant to assist in implementation of the Ind-AS. Further, the Bank has procured\nthe required software and onboarded the vendor for software implementation of Indian Accounting Standards (Ind-AS).\nThe Bank has also constituted a Steering Committee to oversee the progress made and the Audit Committee of the Board\nis being apprised of the same from time to time. Further, in terms of DO.DBR.BP.No.2535/21.07.001/2017-18 dated 13th\nSeptember 2017, the Bank had been submitting Proforma Ind AS financial statements to the RBI on quarterly basis till 31st","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · FY2026","document_date":null,"document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c1611","section":"Cash Flow Statement","tag":"cashflow","page":631,"text":"September 2017, the Bank had been submitting Proforma Ind AS financial statements to the RBI on quarterly basis till 31st\nMarch 2021. Thereafter, in term of RBI’s (Department of Regulation) mail dated 8th August 2021, bank has been advised\nto submit Proforma Ind AS financial statements on half yearly basis. Last proforma financials for the half year ended 30th\nSeptember 2025 was submitted to RBI vide letter dated 26th November 2025.\n279 Union Bank of India | Integrated Annual Report 2025-26\nGRI Index Capitals Strategy About\nSchedule 18 – Notes to Accounts\ng. Payment of DICGC Insurance Premium\n(` in crore)\nParticulars FY 2025-26 FY 2024-25\nPayment of DICGC Insurance Premium (Inclusive of GST) 1,763.09 1,688.47\nArrears in payment of DICGC premium (Inclusive of GST) -- --\nh. Disclosure on amortization of expenditure on account of enhancement in family pension of employees of banks:\nThere is no amortised expenditure in the financial statements on account of family pension scheme.\ni. Disclosure on Letters of Comfort (LOCs) issued by the Banks:\n(` in crore)\nParticulars FY 2025-26 FY 2024-25\nLetter of Comfort outstanding at beginning of the year -- --\nAdd: Issued during the year -- --\nLess: Expired during the year -- --\nOutstanding at the end of the year -- --","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · FY2026","document_date":null,"document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c1612","section":"Cash Flow Statement","tag":"cashflow","page":632,"text":"Outstanding at the end of the year -- --\nIn terms of RBI/2017-18/139 A.P. (DIR Series) Circular No. 20 dated March 13, 2018, issuance of Letter of Undertaking (LoUs) and\nLetters of Comfort (LoCs) for Trade Credits for imports into India has been discontinued.\nj. Portfolio-level information on the use of funds raised from green deposits\nGreen Deposits\nParticulars FY 2025-26 FY 2024-25 Cumulative\nTotal green deposits raised (A) 0.24 29.05 29.29\nUse of green deposit funds\n1. Renewable Energy 0.24 29.05 29.29\n2. Energy Efficiency -- -- --\n3. Clean Transportation -- -- --\n4. Climate Change Adaptation -- -- --\n5. Sustainable Water and Waste Management -- -- --\n6. Pollution Prevention and Control -- -- --\n7. Green Buildings -- -- --\n8. Sustainable Management of Living Natural Resources and Land Use -- -- --\n9. Terrestrial and Aquatic Biodiversity Conservation -- -- --\nTotal Green Deposit funds allocated (B = Sum of 1 to 9) 0.24 29.05 29.29\nAmount of Green Deposit funds not allocated (C = A – B) -- -- --\nDetails of the temporary allocation of green deposit proceeds pending their allocation to the eligible green activities/projects\n-- -- ----\nNOTE – Total Green Deposit raised during FY 25-26 is ` 0.24 crore (F.Y. 2024-25 is ` 29.05 Cr ). Total outstanding balance under Union Green Deposit Scheme is ` 8.21 Crore as on 31.03.2026 (Outstanding as on 31.03.2025 is ` 11.99 Cr).","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · FY2026","document_date":null,"document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c1613","section":"Cash Flow Statement","tag":"cashflow","page":632,"text":"NOTE – Total Green Deposit raised during FY 25-26 is ` 0.24 crore (F.Y. 2024-25 is ` 29.05 Cr ). Total outstanding balance under Union Green Deposit Scheme is ` 8.21 Crore as on 31.03.2026 (Outstanding as on 31.03.2025 is ` 11.99 Cr).\n280 Union Bank of India | Integrated Annual Report 2025-26\nFinancials Reports Notice\n15. Disclosures as per Accounting Standards issued by The Institute of Chartered Accountants of India (ICAI)\na. NET PROFIT OR LOSS FOR THE PERIOD, PRIOR PERIOD ITEMS AND CHANGES IN ACCOUNTING POLICIES (AS 5)\ni) During the year there were no material and prior period income / expenditure items.\nii) There is no change in significant accounting policies adopted during the current Financial year as compared to those\nfollowed in previous Financial year.\nb. REVENUE RECOGNITION (AS 9)\nIncome and Expenditure have been accounted for on accrual basis except certain items of income are recognized on\nrealization basis as per Accounting Policy no.3.4 of Schedule 17 of Significant Accounting Policies.\nc. EMPLOYEE BENEFITS (AS 15 - REVISED)\nI. Short Term Employment Benefits:\nThe undiscounted amounts of short-term employee benefits (e.g. medical benefits) payable wholly within twelve\nmonths of rendering the service are treated as short term and recognized during the period in which the employee\nrendered the service.\nII. Long Term Employee Benefits:\na. Defined Contribution Plans:","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · FY2026","document_date":null,"document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c1614","section":"Cash Flow Statement","tag":"cashflow","page":633,"text":"a. Defined Contribution Plans:\nThe Bank operates a new pension scheme (NPS) for all officers/employees joining the Bank on or after 1st April, 2010,\nwhich is a defined contribution plan, such new joinees not being entitled to become members of the existing Pension\nScheme. As per the scheme, the covered employees contribute 10% of their basic pay plus dearness allowance to\nthe scheme together with 14% contribution from the Bank. Pending completion of registration procedures of the\nemployees concerned, these contributions retained with the Bank. The Bank recognizes such annual contributions in\nthe year to which they relate. Upon receipt of the Permanent Retirement Account Number (PRAN), the consolidated\ncontribution amounts are transferred to the NPS trust.\nThe Bank has Defined Contribution Pension Scheme (DCPS) applicable to all categories of officers and employees\njoining the Bank on or after April 1, 2010. The scheme is managed by National Pension Scheme (NPS) Trust under\nthe aegis of the Pension Fund Regulatory and Development Authority. Protean eGov Technologies Limited (earlier\nknown as National Securities Depository Limited) has been appointed as the Central Record Keeping Agency for the\nNPS. During F.Y. 2025-26, the Bank has contributed ` 767.52 crores (Previous Year ` 704.53 crore) to NPS.\nb. Defined Benefit Plan:","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · FY2026","document_date":null,"document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c1615","section":"Cash Flow Statement","tag":"cashflow","page":633,"text":"b. Defined Benefit Plan:\nGratuity, Pension and Leave Encashment are defined benefit plans. These are provided for on the basis of an actuarial\nvaluation as per Accounting Standard-15 “Employee Benefit” issued by the Institute of Chartered Accountants of\nIndia, made at the end of each financial year, based on the projected unit credit method. Actuarial gains/losses are\nimmediately taken to the Profit & Loss account.\nDefined Benefit Plans – Employee’s Pension plan and Gratuity plan:\nThe Bank has accounted for employee benefits as per Accounting Standards issued by the Institute of Chartered\nAccountants of India, as per actuarial valuation report for the year ended March 31, 2026.\n281 Union Bank of India | Integrated Annual Report 2025-26\nGRI Index Capitals Strategy About\nSchedule 18 – Notes to Accounts\n(` in crore)\nPension Plans Gratuity Plans\nParticulars\nFY 2025-26 FY 2024-25 FY 2025-26 FY 2024-25\nChange in the present value of the defined benefit obligation\nOpening defined benefit obligation as at 1st April 33,363.67 31,555.91 3,981.38 3,602.00\nInterest Cost 2,352.14 2,284.65 272.72 259.70\nCurrent Service Cost 241.81 242.52 212.41 227.54\nPast Service Cost (Vested Benefit Amortized) -- -- -- --\nPast Service Cost (Vested Benefit) -- -- -- --\nLiability Transfer in -- -- -- --\nLiability Transfer out -- -- -- --\nBenefit paid (2,582.89) (2,568.00) (258.89) (327.73)","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · FY2026","document_date":null,"document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c1616","section":"Cash Flow Statement","tag":"cashflow","page":634,"text":"Benefit paid (2,582.89) (2,568.00) (258.89) (327.73)\nActuarial (Gain)/loss on obligation –due to change\nIn the financial assumption (2,699.80) 572.70 (377.77) 143.13\nin demographic assumption 2,241.03 -- -- --\nActuarial (Gain) / Loss on obligations 1,759.08 1,275.89 310.24 76.74\nClosing defined benefit obligation as at 31st March 34,675.04 33,363.67 4,140.09 3,981.38\nTable of Fair value of Plan Assets:\nOpening fair value of plan assets as at 1st April 33,346.51 31,140.21 3,994.75 3,457.68\nExpected return on Plan Assets 2,350.93 2,254.55 273.64 249.30\nContributions 1,816.21 2,240.99 461.61 574.37\nTransfer from Other Company -- -- -- --\nTransfer to Other Company -- -- -- --\nBenefit paid (2,582.89) (2,568.00) (258.89) (327.73)\nActuarial (Gain)/loss on Plan Assets (85.79) 278.76 (23.94) 41.13\nClosing fair value of plan assets as at 31st March 34,844.97 33,346.51 4,447.17 3,994.75\nActuarial (Gain)/loss on obligation for the period 1,300.31 1,848.59 (67.53) 219.87\nActuarial (Gain)/loss on Plan Assets 85