io of their respective Segment Assets.\n5. Figure of previous period have been regrouped/reclassified wherever necessary.\n12 RELATED PARTY DISCLOSURES (AS-18) (Parent Bank)\n12.1 List of Related Parties\na) Subsidiaries\n• Union Asset Management Co. Pvt. Ltd.\n• Union Trustee Company Pvt. Ltd.\n• Union Bank of India (UK) Ltd.\n• Andhra Bank Financial Services Ltd.\n• UBI Services Ltd.\n338 Union Bank of India | Integrated Annual Report 2025-26\nFinancials Reports Notice\nb) Joint Venture\n• Star Union Dai-Ichi Life Insurance Co. Ltd.\n• ASREC (India) Ltd.\n• India International Bank (Malaysia) Berhad (till 06.11.2025).\nc) Associate\n• Andhra Pradesh Grameena Bank\n12.2 Key Management Personnel (` in Crore)\nName Designation Remuneration paid for the Year ended 31st March 2026\nShri. Asheesh Pandey Managing Director & CEO (from 30.09.2025) 0.22\nShri Nitesh Ranjan Executive Director 0.45\nShri Ramasubramanian S Executive Director 0.56\nShri Sanjay Rudra Executive Director 0.37\nShri Amresh Prasad Executive Director (from 24.11.2025) 0.16\nMs. A. Manimekhalai Managing Director & CEO (till 02.06.2025) 0.08","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · FY2026","document_date":null,"document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c1750","section":"Balance Sheet","tag":"balance","page":691,"text":"Ms. A. Manimekhalai Managing Director & CEO (till 02.06.2025) 0.08\nShri Pankaj Dwivedi Executive Director (till 24.06.2025) 0.09 Parties with whom transactions were entered into during the year\nNo disclosure is required in respect of related parties, which are “State controlled Enterprises” as per paragraph 9 of\nAccounting Standard (AS) 18. Further, in terms of paragraph 6 of AS 18, transactions in the nature of Banker – Customer\nrelationship have not been disclosed including those with Key Management Personnel and relatives of Key Management\nPersonnel.\nAs per the RBI Master Direction, KMPs are construed to be the Whole Time Directors of the Bank.\n13 CONTINGENT LIABLITIES (AS-29)\nContingent liabilities referred to in Schedule-12 at S. No.(I) & (VI) (i) are dependent upon the outcome of court/arbitration/\nout of court settlement, the amount being called up, terms of contractual obligations, devolvement and raising of demand\nby parties concerned, disposal of appeals respectively. During the year, certain contingent liabilities were reclassified as\ncontra items in accordance with the Bank’s review and reporting framework.”\n14 EARNING PER SHARE (AS-20)\nBasic earnings per equity share are computed by dividing net profit after tax by the weighted average number of equity","doc_type":"annual_report","document":"Annual report · FY2026","document_date":null,"document_rank":0,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"c1751","section":"Balance Sheet","tag":"balance","page":691,"text":"Basic earnings per equity share are computed by dividing net profit after tax by the weighted average number of equity\nshares outstanding during the year. The diluted earnings per equity share is computed using the weighted average number\nof equity shares and weighted average number of diluted potential equity shares outstanding during the year.\nThe computation of earnings per share is given below:\nParticulars FY 2025-26 FY 2024-25\nNumber of Equity shares at the beginning of the year 7,63,36,05,607 7,63,36,05,607\nNumber of Equity shares issued during the year -- --\nNumber of Equity shares outstanding at the end of the year 7,63,36,05,607 7,63,36,05,607\nWeighted Average Number of Equity Shares used in computing Basic Earnings\nper share 7,63,36,05,607 7,63,36,05,607\n339 Union Bank of India | Integrated Annual Report 2025-26\nGRI Index Capitals Strategy About\nSchedule 18 – Notes to Accounts\nParticulars FY 2025-26 FY 2024-25\nWeighted Average Number of Shares used in computing diluted Earnings per\nshare 7,63,36,05,607 7,63,36,05,607\nNet Profit/(Loss) Rs. in Crore 19,430.20 18,026.95\nBasic Earnings per share (Rs.) 25.45 23.62\nDiluted Earnings per share (R