:"other","page":7,"text":"Customer\nOptimization\ndevelopment\npositive finance\nRisk\nDividend distribution\nworkforce\nservice\nGreen finance\nCompliance\nCompliance\nExpansion\nInclusive\nmanagement\nCredit growth: 12.50%\nCustomer satisfaction\nDevelopment\nDevelopment\nRenewable\nworkplace\nRenewable\nPartnerships\nCybersecurity\nQuality\nTransparency\nenergy support\nDeposit growth: 3.50%\nDigital Skill\nInvestment\nEmployee engagement\nSkills\nNet-zero 2035\nEngagement\nCarbon\nenhancement\nInclusive\nBranch network: 8,700\nRegulatory compliance\nreduction\nculture\nOperational efficiency\nSource: Company Filings, Offering Circular. Note: FX: US$ 1= 94.6626 (FBIL closing rate as of June 30, 2026).\nKey Credit\nFinancial Inclusion\nAppendix: Financial\nHighlights Union Bank\n& ESG Asset Quality & Capital Adequacy\nOverview\nStatements\nBoard of Directors\nAsheesh Pandey – Managing Director and CEO\n Mr. Pandey holds a degree in Mechanical Engineering, a postgraduate qualification in Management with specialization in Finance & Marketing, and is an alumnus of IIM Bangalore.\n He brings 27+ years of banking experience across credit, treasury, international banking, operations and digital transformation, and previously served as Executive Director at Bank of Maharashtra and Chief General Manager at Union Bank.\nNitesh Ranjan – Executive Director\nRamasubramanian S – Executive Director\nAmresh Prasad – Executive Director","doc_type":"presentation","document":"Investor presentation · Aug 2026","document_date":"2026-08-15","document_rank":2,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"p2-c19","section":"Front matter","tag":"other","page":8,"text":"Amresh Prasad – Executive Director\n Mr. Ramasubramanian holds a Bachelor of Science degree and is a CAIIB-qualified banker.\n Mr. Prasad is a graduate in Chemistry and a CAIIB- qualified banker.\n Mr. Ranjan holds a postgraduate degree in Economics and has completed the Leadership Development Programme at IIM Bangalore.\n He brings 25+ years of experience across corporate credit, MSME, retail banking, international credit and forex, and previously served as Chief General Manager at Canara Bank.\n He has 32+ years of banking experience across corporate credit, credit monitoring and transaction banking, and previously served as Chief General Manager at Punjab National Bank.\n He has 20+ years of banking experience and has held leadership roles across treasury, strategy, economics & digital transformation at Union Bank.\nDebasish Prusty - GOI Nominee\nPrakash Baliarsingh - RBI Nominee\nPriti Jay Rao - Shareholder Director\nPrakash Chandra Kandpal – Shareholder Director\n Dr. Prusty holds a Ph.D. in Management and an M.Phil. in Environmental Sciences.\n Mr. Baliarsingh holds a postgraduate degree in Political Science, an M.Sc. (Finance) and is a CAIIB-qualified banker.\n Dr. Rao holds an M.Sc. in Mathematics with specialization in Computer Science from IIT Bombay.\n Mr. Kandpal holds an M.A. (Economics) and a Master’s in Financial Management from JBIMS Mumbai.","doc_type":"presentation","document":"Investor presentation · Aug 2026","document_date":"2026-08-15","document_rank":2,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"p2-c20","section":"Front matter","tag":"other","page":8,"text":" Mr. Kandpal holds an M.A. (Economics) and a Master’s in Financial Management from JBIMS Mumbai.\n An IAS officer, he has 26+ years of experience in public finance and policy formulation and currently serves as Additional Secretary, Department of Financial Services.\n He brings 30+ years of experience with the RBI across banking regulation and supervision, including as Chief General Manager, Dept. of Regulation.\n She has 26+ years of experience in technology services, digital transformation and automation, & serves on the boards of multiple technology companies.\n He has 36+ years of experience across banking, insurance and asset management, including leadership roles at SBI & SBI General Insurance.\nSource: Company Website, Offering Circular.\nKey Credit\nFinancial Inclusion\nAppendix: Financial\nHighlights Union Bank\n& ESG Asset Quality & Capital Adequacy\nOverview\nStatements\nSustained Growth in Earnings with Expanding Profitability and Returns\nNet Interest Income Operating Profit Net Profit\n($ mn) ($ mn) ($ mn)\n2,980 3,284 3,023\n3,863 3,931 3,873\n1,442 1,900 1,975\n1,060\nFY24 FY25 FY26 Q1 FY27\nFY24 FY25 FY26 Q1 FY27\nFY24 FY25 FY26 Q1 FY27\nSustained above $3,800mn since FY24 Highest-ever quarterly operating profit of $845mn\nExpanded at a ~17% CAGR during FY24-26\nRoA % RoE %\n1.03% 1.26% 1.25% 1.36%\n17.23%\n17.20%\n15.86%\n15.58%\nFY24 FY25 FY26 Q1 FY27\nFY24 FY25 FY26 Q1 FY27","doc_type":"presentation","document":"Investor presentation · Aug 2026","document_date":"2026-08-15","document_rank":2,"page_kind":"pdf"},{"id":"p2-c21","section":"Front matter","tag":"other","page":9,"text":"FY24 FY25 FY26 Q1 FY27\nImproved by 33 bps to 1.36% Expanded by 165 bps to 17.23%\nSource: Company Filings, Offering Circular. Note: All figures represent Standalone Financials. FX: US$ 1= 94.6626 (FBIL closing rate as of June 30, 2026).\nKey Credit\nFinancial Inclusion\nAppendix: Financial\nHighlights Union Bank\n& ESG Asset Quality & Capital Adequacy\nOverview\nStatements\nStrong Asset Quality Underpinned by Lower NPAs and High Provision Coverage\nGNPA NNPA\n($ mn) ($ mn)\n4,553 3,734 3,212 3,073\n631 535 530\nFY24 FY25 FY26 Q1 FY27\nFY24 FY25 FY26 Q1 FY27\nReduced by $1,480mn Reduced by $420mn\nGNPA % & NNPA %\nPCR %\n4.76%\n94.61% 95.03% 95.05%\n3.60% 2.82% 2.65%\n92.69%\n1.03% 0.63% 0.48% 0.47%\nFY24 FY25 FY26 Q1 FY27 GNPA % NNPA %\nFY24 FY25 FY26 Q1 FY27\nStrengthened by 236 bps to 95.05%\nGNPA / NNPA improved by 211 bps / 56 bps\nSource: Company Filings, Offering Circular. Note: FX: US$ 1= 94.6626 (FBIL closing rate as of June 30, 2026).\nKey Credit\nFinancial Inclusion\nAppendix: Financial\nHighlights Union Bank\n& ESG Asset Quality & Capital Adequacy\nOv